# launch-hush-planet-chapter.rish -- print the loop for HUSH, Dream's planet.
#
# Hush is Dream's own night twin made a working hand: the star holds the systems core as Codex
# on the pier, and its planet runs CLAUDE CODE ON THE FRAMEWORK LAPTOP, working the hands-on
# systems half beside it -- POND COMPLETING THE AI-JAIL ENCLOSURE under the accrete-only
# documentation boundary, and the STANDING ADAPTATION GRANT (bash to Rishi, HTML to Brush,
# Python to Glow). A planet defers to its star where lanes brush: Pond leans on Caravan's
# capability and address-space pieces, and a change wanted inside caravan/ or tally/ is Dream's
# lane -- a line on the card. Lane seated by the role swap of 20260827.155213 on Keaton's word.
# Charter: active-designing/20260827-155213_the-six-bodies-and-the-closed-stacks.md.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-hush-planet-chapter.rish

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the durable memory lives.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the living charter this seat lives in must exist.
let charter = run ["test" "-f" "active-designing/20260827-155213_the-six-bodies-and-the-closed-stacks.md"]
assert charter.ok else "the six-bodies charter is missing"

say "HUSH -- Dream's planet (the star's own night twin, made a hand)"
say "==============================================================="
say ""
say "Host: CLAUDE CODE ON THE FRAMEWORK LAPTOP, a terminal loop. The shared"
say "discipline lives on the living card; the lane lives in the six-bodies"
say "charter; both are read fresh every lap."
say ""
say "0) PRECONDITIONS, once per machine: this repo cloned with the xy remote;"
say "   git submodule update --init --recursive; jq for the readable stream"
say "   (the distribution package, or drop the jq tail and raw NDJSON scrolls)."
say "   Power is a preference, never a gate: the repo is the durable memory, a"
say "   cut lap costs only its uncommitted work, the next round-open pull"
say "   resumes the thread."
say ""
say "1) BYPASS STANDING (once, gitignored): in .claude/settings.local.json set"
say "   permissions.defaultMode = bypassPermissions -- or keep the flag below."
say "   Claude refuses the flag as root; run as a plain user."
say ""
say "2) SMOKE TEST:"
say "   claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max -p 'reply with exactly: pong'"
say ""
let seat_prompt = "First read context/KYRI.md and context/GAUGE_STYLE.md so you are Kyri and write and reason in Gauge Guidance from the first token -- first rule, do not be too smart about it; then read construction/ITINERARY.md whole and honor every directive in its INNER LOOP Standing block (roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, the council rota row N mod 5 advancing by hand past a repeat, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, and the READ SCOPE: walk the open shelves, fetch a closed stack only by a named path -- MAP.md is the walk, never an ls of the root); then the newest day shelf named at the top of session-logs/README.md and its top three rows, with the newest recommend line, to pick up the running thread -- and write this laps own log BORN ON ITS DAYS SHELF, session-logs/date/YYYYMMDD/, its row prepended to date/README-index-YYYYMMDD.md. You are HUSH, Dreams own planet -- the stars night twin made a working hand -- Claude Code on the Framework laptop. Your lane (the role swap, Keatons word 20260827) is the hands-on systems half: Pond completing the ai-jail enclosure -- code, CLI interface, witnesses -- under the ACCRETE-ONLY GATE BOUNDARY: every markdown that instructs or references ai-jail stays unmolted, accreted beside and never rewritten, until the replacement is tested and audited end to end (safe, then secure, then performing, then a joy); the switchover of instructions and references is its own later round behind that audit. You also hold the STANDING ADAPTATION GRANT: adapt non-Rye files as your lane touches them -- bash and sh into Rishi, HTML into Brush, Python into Glow -- each adaptation its own witnessed round, elders kept until successors prove GREEN; a Glow-language feature an adaptation wants belongs to Sounds language custody and becomes an ITINERARY line. A planet defers to its star where lanes brush: what Dream holds -- caravan/, tally/, the constellation table on the pier -- stays Dreams, and a find there becomes a line in ITINERARY rather than your lap. Open every lap with ListAgents and name any peer before a file moves -- the charter law from REDS %291; commits stay path-limited and the amend stands behind the empty-index check. Sibling bodies: Mind with its planet Mystery (Brushstroke-Surf design; the Android and AppImage surface), Sound with its planet Silence (the interface and infrastructure halves of Grain in Glow, language custody Sounds); everything in the DJINN design lead stays custody gate %6. The charter is active-designing/20260827-155213_the-six-bodies-and-the-closed-stacks.md. Send the twice-pulled way with the remote named xy on this clone -- pull first, package, fetch again, rebase and re-verify hot when it moved, never force -- and the public seed stays a manual gate: never run publish-seed.sh from this bench. STOP at the custody gates in ITINERARY; if only those gates remain, run the shell command  touch .loop-gates-only  and print GATES-ONLY, then stop. ty every1 baton prin recur"

say "3) ONE ROUND, ONCE -- one lap, the same seat and renderer, no loop, no sentinel:"
say ""
say "sh tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh; claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max --output-format stream-json --verbose -p '${seat_prompt}' | tee /tmp/hush_lap.jsonl | jq -Rrj -f tools/s/stream_render.jq"
say ""
say "4) THE LOOP -- one line, copy whole (GNU date first, BSD spelling as the fallback):"
say ""
say "D=$(TZ=America/New_York date -d 'tomorrow 15:00' +%s 2>/dev/null || TZ=America/New_York date -v+1d -v15H -v0M -v0S +%s); while [ $(date +%s) -lt $D ]; do rm -f .loop-gates-only; sh tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh || { echo 'ROUND-OPEN: fetch refused; retrying in 60s'; sleep 60; continue; }; claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max --output-format stream-json --verbose -p '${seat_prompt}' | tee /tmp/hush_lap.jsonl | jq -Rrj -f tools/s/stream_render.jq; [ -f .loop-gates-only ] && { echo GATES-ONLY: loop paused; break; }; sleep 20; done; echo Hush loop ended at $(TZ=America/New_York date)"
say ""
say "5) STREAMING: the tee-then-jq tail IS the readable terminal -- one line per"
say "   tool call, a dot per silent half-minute, text as it lands."
say ""
say "6) WHY A FILE SENTINEL: stream-json echoes the prompt, which contains the"
say "   words GATES-ONLY, so a grep on the stream would false-stop after one lap."
say ""
say "7) CUSTODY: the gates in ITINERARY stay MANUAL -- funds and keys, provisioning"
say "   and paying, the maintainer's own identity, and the public seed."
say ""
say "MANY HANDS (granted 20260828, Keaton's word): this seat may spin up multiple"
say "CLI agents and manage them -- subagents, worker sessions, parallel claude or"
say "codex children -- when dividing a lap pays. Every standing law rides into"
say "each child: custody gates stay MANUAL, one writer per checkout (the %291"
say "habit -- ListAgents, name the peer, path-limited commits), and the parent"
say "seat answers for what its children stage."
say ""
say "GREEN: Hush recipe printed -- the star holds the core, and its planet closes the enclosure around it."
